-- title:
--   Local components patch to an element of DotimesA_ℚ^f
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be a ring equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, and let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $D$ which is finitely generated and whose $\mathbb{Q}$-span, as a subset of $D$, is all of $D$. Let $x$ be a family assigning to each height-one prime $v$ of the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ an element $x_v \in D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$, where $\mathbb{Q}_v$ denotes the $v$-adic completion of $\mathbb{Q}$. Assume that for all but finitely many $v$ the element $x_v$ lies in [`Submodule.localBox`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) $\Lambda$ $v$, that is, in the additive subgroup of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by the pure tensors $z \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} c$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $c$ in the valuation ring $\mathbb{Z}_v$ of $\mathbb{Q}_v$. The conclusion is that there exists $y \in D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$, where $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$ relative to $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, such that for every height-one prime $v$ one has $\mathrm{finiteAdeleEvalAt}\,D\,v\,(y) = x_v$; here [`Submodule.finiteAdeleEvalAt`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L36) is the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra homomorphism $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f} \to D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ obtained by tensoring the identity of $D$ with evaluation of a finite adele at $v$. Only the existence of such a $y$ is asserted; no uniqueness claim is made.
--
--   This is the surjectivity half of the classical local–global description of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ as the restricted product of the completions $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ with respect to the local lattices $\Lambda \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}} \mathbb{Z}_v$. It is the tool by which place-by-place constructions of local elements are assembled into a single finite idele, and it is invoked in the Cerednik–Drinfeld and level-structure computations, for instance in the analysis of Eichler orders and of the Hecke sets attached to a level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Submodule_exists_forall_finiteAdeleEvalAt_eq.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox
import Definitions.Def_Submodule_LocalBox

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open scoped TensorProduct
open IsDedekindDomain NumberField

theorem Submodule.exists_forall_finiteAdeleEvalAt_eq
    {D : Type*} [Ring D] [Algebra ℚ D]
    (Λ : Submodule ℤ D) (hfg : Λ.FG) (hspan : Submodule.span ℚ (Λ : Set D) = ⊤)
    (x : (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 ℚ)) → D ⊗[ℚ] v.adicCompletion ℚ)
    (hx : ∀ᶠ v in Filter.cofinite, x v ∈ Submodule.localBox Λ v) :
    ∃ y : D ⊗[ℚ] FiniteAdeleRing (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ,
      ∀ v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 ℚ), Submodule.finiteAdeleEvalAt D v y = x v := by sorry
